config PCIE_EP_CDNS
	bool
	help
	  Register level support for the Cadence PCIe controller in endpoint
	  mode, used by SoC specific glue drivers.

config PCIE_EPC_RK3399
	bool "Rockchip RK3399 PCIe endpoint controller"
	default y
	depends on DT_HAS_ROCKCHIP_RK3399_PCIE_EP_ENABLED
	depends on SYSCON && RESET && CLOCK_CONTROL && GPIO
	select PCIE_EPC
	select PCIE_EP_CDNS
	select PCIE_RK3399_PORT
	help
	  The Cadence based PCIe controller of the RK3399 in endpoint mode,
	  on the EPC API: header, BARs, outbound windows (32 x 1 MiB, region
	  0 for MSI), MSI and INTx, PERST# and link events. MSI-X is hidden
	  (not functional on this silicon). With PCIE_ROLE the same
	  controller is the root complex when that role is saved.

config PCIE_EPC_RK3399_SRIOV
	bool "SR-IOV strap (1 PF + up to 8 VFs)"
	depends on PCIE_EPC_RK3399
	help
	  Set sr_iov_en in PCIE_CLIENT_CONFIG (with ari_en, always set) in
	  endpoint mode, so the core exposes its SR-IOV capability. VF BARs,
	  inbound windows and MSI per VF are not handled yet: this only shows
	  the capability and its reset values to the host.
